"{\"url\":\"https://www.microcision.com/cmm-programmer\",\"title\":\"CMM PROGRAMMER | Microcision\",\"desc\":null,\"og\":null,\"robots\":null,\"imgs\":[\"Microcision logo.png | 31e942_ef154a865afe4fa79723417987ebbaeb~mv2.png\"],\"form\":[],\"iframes\":[],\"sha256\":\"dd430f38182d3f66f2ad18eb7f45d374835d7c3d4995323dd6b67c312684d862\",\"text\":\"Skip to Main Content\\n\\nHOME\\n\\nSERVICES\\n\\nABOUT\\n\\nEXPANSION\\n\\nCAREERS\\n\\nCONTACT\\n\\nCMM Programmer\\n\\n\\u00a0\\n\\nMICROCISION is a worldwide leader in medical device implant and instrument manufacturing. Headquartered in a completely modern facility, next to Cooper River Park, our company is seeking outstanding individuals to join our team as CMM Programmers.\\n\\nEstablished over 50 years and with over 50 CNCs, Microcision is experiencing rapid growth with the worlds most advanced medical device companies as its\\u2019 customers. Our manufacturing company utilizes the latest models of equipment and programming software.\\n\\n\\u200b\\n\\nIf you are looking for a challenging career, with very competitive salary, benefits, 401k and great PTO, apply NOW.\\n\\nPrimary duties and responsibilities include:\\n\\nProgram set-up and operate CMM and Optical measuring machines.\\n\\nSet-up CMM inspection for other operators / shifts.\\n\\nPerform first piece, in process, and final inspection of machined parts.\\n\\nAssist machine programmers and set-up personnel to optimize both milling and screw machine set-up time and machine utilization.\\n\\nTrain personnel to operate CMM and Optical measuring machines.\\n\\nCompletion of internal and customer required quality documentation.\\n\\n\\u00a0\\n\\nCandidate shall meet the following requirements:\\n\\n(3) years minimum CMM programming and operational experience (B & S / Hexagon PC DMIS preferred). Alternate CMM experience will be considered.\\n\\nOptical Measuring device experience (OGP, Keyence, Nikon or similar).\\n\\nBackground in Quality/Mechanical Engineering a plus\\n\\nBackground in Geometric Dimensioning & Tolerancing\\n\\nSPC (MiniTab) experience a plus.\\n\\nCapability to use all standard measuring tools such as optical comparators calipers, micrometers, go/no-go and thread gauges, surface plate instruments.\\n\\nAble to use a computer and have a working knowledge of Microsoft Office.(Outlook / Excel / Word / Power Point / Visio)\\n\\nAbility to multi-task and be flexible in a fast-paced manufacturing environment.\\n\\nBasic understanding of any of the following: ISO-13485:2016 , ISO 9001:2015 , TS16949, AS9100C, 21CFR820 quality systems.\\n\\n\\u200b\\n\\nHours- 1st shift or 2nd shift/ Swing shift 10:00 am to 8:30 pm available if preferred.\\n\\nWe offer a competitive salary, medical and dental insurance, 401k, overtime, and advancement. EOE.\\n\\n\\u200b\\n\\nJob Type: Full-time\\n\\nPay: $28.00 - $30.00 per hour\\n\\n\\u00a9 2022\\u00a0by Microcision LLC\"}"
